{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgavyJK18bXQKYZhAfk1i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `factorialAcc_correct`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe theorem can't be proved by induction as written, because the accumulator changes at each step. So I first proved a more general helper lemma:\n\n```lean\ntheorem factorialAcc_eq (n a : Nat) : factorialAcc n a = a * factorial n := by\n  induction n generalizing a with\n  | zero => simp [factorialAcc, factorial]\n  | succ n ih =>\n    simp only [factorialAcc, factorial, ih]\n    rw [Nat.mul_assoc]\n\ntheorem factorialAcc_correct (n : Nat) : factorialAcc n 1 = factorial n := by\n  rw [factorialAcc_eq, Nat.one_mul]\n```\n\n- **Helper lemma:** I proved it by induction on `n` for every accumulator `a` at once. In the step case, the goal reduces to `a * (n+1) * n! = a * ((n+1) * n!)`, which is just regrouping the multiplication (`Nat.mul_assoc`).\n- **Main theorem:** setting `a = 1` and simplifying `1 * factorial n` to `factorial n` gives the result."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":7971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":669},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23e2c08f-67df-443e-8bbf-8e16ef7fdbc8","uuid":"a88ed5c5-0034-4f9f-8d46-b8027247ea77","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:17:18.286Z","request_id":"req_011CgavyJ5s9926SYGVqLKiv"}
